<title>USA: Disney taps three banks for $5 billion refinancing.</title>
<headline>Disney taps three banks for $5 billion refinancing.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co. has tapped BankAmerica Corp., Citicorp's Citibank and Credit Suisse for a $5 billion refinancing bank loan, banking sources said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The loan will refinance a $12 billion credit facility the entertainment giant took out last year for its $19 billion acquisition of Capital Cities/ABC television network, the sources said.</p>
<p>Disney's stock gained 12.5 cents to $62.875 in midday trading on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
